I SEE SOMETHING NATURALLY
THAT KIND OF WORKS FOR HER.

227
00:08:36,316 --> 00:08:37,683
SARA--OPENING UP HER MOUTH.

228
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:39,686
SHE'S LIKE A FISH.

229
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:45,325
OH, HERE SHE COMES.

230
00:08:45,325 --> 00:08:46,126
MISS BLING-BLING.

231
00:08:46,126 --> 00:08:47,227
MISS CAMILLE.

232
00:08:47,227 --> 00:08:48,561
I THINK HER WALK,
WITH A FEW ADJUSTMENTS,

233
00:08:48,561 --> 00:08:51,231
SHE'LL BE GREAT.

234
00:08:51,231 --> 00:08:52,599
OH, SEE, I...

235
00:08:52,599 --> 00:08:58,038
SEE, YOU KNOW, BLACK GIRLS
ALWAYS HAVE TO GIVE THAT EXTRA.

236
00:08:58,038 --> 00:09:00,040
I AIN'T MAD AT YOU.

237
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,808
Yoanna: CAMILLE PUTS ON
A SHOW, AND I THINK

238
00:09:01,808 --> 00:09:03,443
EVERYONE RECOGNIZES THAT.

239
00:09:03,443 --> 00:09:04,477
Camille: I'M JUST FOCUSED
AND DETERMINED

240
00:09:04,477 --> 00:09:05,945
ON WHAT I WANNA DO.

241
00:09:05,945 --> 00:09:09,783
MAYBE YOANNA DIDN'T LIKE THAT
ABOUT ME AND MAYBE WISHED THAT

242
00:09:09,783 --> 00:09:12,819
SHE COULD BE MORE COMFORTABLE
IN HER SKIN AS I AM IN MINE.

243
00:09:14,654 --> 00:09:18,858
J.: WHOO!
WE GONNA HAVE FUN.

244
00:09:18,858 --> 00:09:20,427
WE ARE GONNA HAVE FUN.

245
00:09:24,964 --> 00:09:28,902
MISS YOANNA,
YOUR WALK REALLY IS AS USELESS

246
00:09:28,902 --> 00:09:31,104
AS A FLASHLIGHT
WITH NO BATTERIES IN THE DARK.

247
00:09:31,104 --> 00:09:31,971
(laughter)

248
00:09:33,373 --> 00:09:34,641
J.: YOANNA, I NEED YOU

249
00:09:34,641 --> 00:09:36,342
TO RELAX THROUGH HERE.

250
00:09:36,342 --> 00:09:39,279
I DON'T WANT YOU TO DO...

251
00:09:39,279 --> 00:09:43,716
(imitating horse whinnying)
(laughter)

252
00:09:43,716 --> 00:09:45,351
J.: NO, WE CAN'T HAVE THAT.

253
00:09:45,351 --> 00:09:48,855
SO I'LL SEE YOU GUYS
AFTER LUNCH, OKAY?

254
00:10:10,009 --> 00:10:11,277
Yoanna: I'M ONE
OF THOSE PEOPLE--

255
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:13,246
IF SOMEONE HAS AN ISSUE
OR MIGHT BE SAYING SOMETHING

256
00:10:13,246 --> 00:10:14,814
ABOUT ME, COME TO ME AND SAY IT,
YOU KNOW?

257
00:10:17,817 --> 00:10:18,818
Yoanna: DON'T START.
Camille: WHAT ARE YOU
HEARING?

258
00:10:18,818 --> 00:10:20,286
Yoanna: DON'T START, CAMILLE.

259
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:21,855
IT'S SO OLD, IT'S SO OLD.

260
00:10:21,855 --> 00:10:23,256
Camille: WHAT ARE YOU
HEARING?
Yoanna: YOUR ATTITUDE.

261
00:10:23,256 --> 00:10:25,024
Camille: IF I HAVE SOMETHING
TO SAY TO YOU,

262
00:10:25,024 --> 00:10:26,326
I WILL SAY IT TO YOUR FACE.

263
00:10:26,326 --> 00:10:28,495
Yoanna: THE LAST COUPLE TIMES
YOU'VE HAD THINGS TO SAY

264
00:10:28,495 --> 00:10:29,729
ABOUT ME, YOU'VE NEVER SAID IT
TO MY FACE,

265
00:10:29,729 --> 00:10:31,931
AND WHEN I
CONFRONTED YOU ABOUT IT--

266
00:10:31,931 --> 00:10:34,667
Camille: I HAVEN'T SAID ANYTHING
TO YOU--

267
00:10:34,667 --> 00:10:36,302
Yoanna: OKAY, OKAY, ENJOY.

268
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:37,670
THANK YOU.

269
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:39,873
Sara: I THINK WHAT'S GOING ON
RIGHT NOW WITH THE WHOLE

270
00:10:39,873 --> 00:10:44,144
CAMILLE/YOANNA SHE SAID,
SHE SAID KINDA STUFF--

271
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:45,211
IT'S JUST THAT.

272
00:10:45,211 --> 00:10:47,447
IT'S JUST HIGH SCHOOL STUFF.

273
00:10:47,447 --> 00:10:49,015
Camille: AND TRUST ME, IF I
HAVE SOMETHING TO SAY TO YOU,

274
00:10:49,015 --> 00:10:50,283
I WILL SAY IT TO YOUR FACE.
Yoanna: I DON'T TRUST YOU.

275
00:10:50,283 --> 00:10:53,119
I DO NOT TRUST YOU.
Camille: BUT THAT'S MY WORD.

276
00:10:53,119 --> 00:10:55,054
Sara: WHOO!

277
00:10:55,054 --> 00:10:56,990
Yoanna: IT'S SO HARD
TO DEAL WITH HER BECAUSE

278
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,691
I THINK SHE'S VERY NEGATIVE.

279
00:10:58,691 --> 00:11:03,062
IT'S HARD TO, LIKE, ASSESS,
LIKE, WHAT'S SHE'S TRYING TO DO.

280
00:11:03,062 --> 00:11:05,331
HONEY, OKAY, END OF DISCUSSION.

281
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:08,234
Camille: I THINK THAT YOANNA
LOOKS AT ME AND SHE SEES THAT

282
00:11:08,234 --> 00:11:10,970
I'M VERY COMFORTABLE IN MY SKIN,
AND MAYBE THAT'S SOMETHING

283
00:11:10,970 --> 00:11:14,073
THAT SHE WISHED
THAT SHE POSSESSED

284
00:11:14,073 --> 00:11:15,608
OR SHE'S TRYING TO GET THERE.

285
00:11:15,608 --> 00:11:18,244
I'M JUST, YOU KNOW,
A GROWN-ASS WOMAN

286
00:11:18,244 --> 00:11:20,346
THAT WANTS TO BE
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,

287
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:21,614
AND THAT'S WHAT I'M HERE TO DO.

288
00:11:21,614 --> 00:11:25,752
BUT I WILL NOT LET SOMEBODY,
YOU KNOW, DISRESPECT ME.

289
00:11:25,752 --> 00:11:27,754
REALLY, LIKE, DON'T PLAY ME.

290
00:11:27,754 --> 00:11:29,756
LIKE, YOU HAVE A BETTER CHANCE
AT PLAYING LOTTO, AND THAT'S

291
00:11:29,756 --> 00:11:31,090
JUST, LIKE, ONE IN A BILLION.

292
00:11:37,330 --> 00:11:38,698
♪♪♪

293
00:11:38,698 --> 00:11:40,133
Jenascia: I'VE HEARD A LOT OF

294
00:11:40,133 --> 00:11:42,869
(bleep) TALKING ABOUT CAMILLE,
AND I BELIEVE THAT THERE'S GONNA

295
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:45,104
BE A LOT OF DRAMA IN THE HOUSE.

296
00:11:45,104 --> 00:11:47,073
Camille: FOR REAL, IF I HAVE
SOMETHING TO SAY TO YOU,

297
00:11:47,073 --> 00:11:48,341
I WILL SAY IT TO YOUR FACE.

298
00:11:48,341 --> 00:11:50,710
Yoanna: SO WHEN I
CONFRONTED YOU ABOUT IT--

299
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:53,479
Camille: I HAVEN'T SAID
ANYTHING TO YOU...

300
00:11:53,479 --> 00:11:55,315
Catie: I LIKE
CAMILLE'S CONFIDENCE.

301
00:11:55,315 --> 00:11:58,418
SHE'S NOT HERE TO MAKE
A BUNCH OF BEST FRIENDS,

302
00:11:58,418 --> 00:11:59,953
BUT SHE'S HERE TO WIN THIS.

303
00:12:02,589 --> 00:12:03,923
TYRA MAIL.

304
00:12:03,923 --> 00:12:05,925
"YOU'VE LEARNED RUNWAY
FROM THE BEST.

305
00:12:05,925 --> 00:12:08,127
NOW IT'S TIME TO PUT IT
TO THE TEST.

306
00:12:08,127 --> 00:12:10,063
YOU'RE MEETING A TOP
NEW YORK DESIGNER TOMORROW.

307
00:12:10,063 --> 00:12:11,531
BE READY BY 10 A.M."

308
00:12:11,531 --> 00:12:13,866
♪ DUM, DUM, DUM ♪♪

309
00:12:17,303 --> 00:12:18,471
Yoanna: TODAY I KNOW WE'RE GONNA
BE MEETING

310
00:12:18,471 --> 00:12:19,539
A FASHION DESIGNER,

311
00:12:19,539 --> 00:12:20,473
BUT I DON'T KNOW WHO
IT'S GOING TO BE

312
00:12:20,473 --> 00:12:22,308
OR WHAT THEY'RE LOOKING FOR.

313
00:12:25,345 --> 00:12:26,212
Carmen: GOOD MORNING, LADIES.

314
00:12:26,212 --> 00:12:27,714
Women: GOOD MORNING.

315
00:12:27,714 --> 00:12:29,215
Carmen: WELL,
I'M CARMEN MARC VALVO,

316
00:12:29,215 --> 00:12:30,783
AND WELCOME TO MY SHOWROOM.

317
00:12:30,783 --> 00:12:32,852
Catie: WHEN I THINK
OF FASHION DESIGNERS,

318
00:12:32,852 --> 00:12:35,989
I THINK OF WET SEAL AND GAP
AND EXPRESS.

319
00:12:35,989 --> 00:12:37,857
Yoanna: CARMEN MARC VALVO
IS ONE OF NEW YORK'S

320
00:12:37,857 --> 00:12:39,525
TOP FASHION DESIGNERS.

321
00:12:39,525 --> 00:12:41,628
THERE'S SUCH QUALITY
AND DETAILING IN HIS WORK.

322
00:12:41,628 --> 00:12:43,496
I'M SO EXCITED TO BE
IN HIS SHOWROOM.

323
00:12:43,496 --> 00:12:45,698
Carmen: YESTERDAY
I UNDERSTAND THAT THEY

324
00:12:45,698 --> 00:12:48,334
TAUGHT YOU HOW TO WALK,
OR THE FINER POINTS OF IT.

325
00:12:48,334 --> 00:12:51,404
WELL, THIS MORNING WE'RE GOING
TO PUT THOSE POINTS TO THE TEST.

326
00:12:51,404 --> 00:12:54,307
THE PERSON I FEEL HAS DONE
THE BEST GETS TO COME

327
00:12:54,307 --> 00:12:55,808
TO MY HOME THIS EVENING.

328
00:12:55,808 --> 00:12:57,110
I'M HAVING A COCKTAIL PARTY.

329
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:58,511
Sara: OH, MY GOD.

330
00:12:58,511 --> 00:13:00,113
Carmen: THERE'LL BE
SOME WONDERFUL PEOPLE THERE--

331
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:02,749
SOME INFLUENTIAL PEOPLE
IN THE FASHION INDUSTRY.

332
00:13:02,749 --> 00:13:04,550
SO LET'S GET STARTED, OKAY?

333
00:13:04,550 --> 00:13:05,918
COME ON, FOLLOW ME.

334
00:13:05,918 --> 00:13:07,186
Yoanna: OF COURSE
I WANNA BE IN HIS HOUSE

335
00:13:07,186 --> 00:13:09,689
AND I WANNA GO AND MEET
ALL THE FASHION PEOPLE THAT WORK

336
00:13:09,689 --> 00:13:10,490
WITH CARMEN MARC VALVO.

337
00:13:10,490 --> 00:13:11,891
I DON'T KNOW.

338
00:13:11,891 --> 00:13:13,860
SOMEONE THERE MIGHT BE ABLE
TO DISCOVER ME AT HIS HOUSE.

339
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:15,862
Carmen: SOME OF
MY CELEBRITY CLIENTELE INCLUDE

340
00:13:15,862 --> 00:13:17,664
LUCY LIU, KIM CATTRALL,
VANESSA WILLIAMS,

341
00:13:17,664 --> 00:13:19,532
JUST TO NAME A FEW.

342
00:13:19,532 --> 00:13:21,668
THESE ARE THE EVENING GOWNS
THAT I HAVE SELECTED FOR YOU.

343
00:13:21,668 --> 00:13:23,636
SOME OF THEM MAY BE
TOO LONG FOR YOU,

344
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:25,038
AND SOME MAY BE TOO SHORT.

345
00:13:25,038 --> 00:13:26,739
THAT HAPPENS.

346
00:13:26,739 --> 00:13:32,545
♪♪♪

347
00:13:32,545 --> 00:13:36,482
Catie: I HAVE THIS PROBABLY
THOUSANDS OF DOLLAR DRESS ON.

348
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:38,151
IT'S CRAZY.

349
00:13:38,151 --> 00:13:39,619
Yoanna: SO MANY THOUGHTS
ARE RUNNING THROUGH MY HEAD.

350
00:13:39,619 --> 00:13:42,288
I'VE SEEN CARMEN MARC VALVO
ON TV, AND HERE I AM

351
00:13:42,288 --> 00:13:43,823
GETTING READY TO WALK FOR HIM?

352
00:13:43,823 --> 00:13:45,925
IT WAS UNBELIEVABLE.

353
00:13:45,925 --> 00:13:48,127
Carmen: WAY TOO MUCH MAKEUP.

354
00:13:48,127 --> 00:13:50,063
IF YOU WERE COMING IN
FOR A CASTING AND YOU LOOKED

355
00:13:50,063 --> 00:13:51,964
THE WAY YOU LOOKED, I PROBABLY
WOULDN'T EVEN ASK YOU

356
00:13:51,964 --> 00:13:53,499
TO PUT ON A DRESS.

357
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:56,402
USUALLY UGLY WOMEN
PUT ON A LOT OF MAKEUP.

358
00:13:56,402 --> 00:13:57,603
COME WITH ME, LADIES.

359
00:13:57,603 --> 00:14:00,239
YOUR JOB IS TO SELL THE DRESS.

360
00:14:00,239 --> 00:14:01,607
YOUR JOB IS TO HAVE
A PHOTOGRAPHER

361
00:14:01,607 --> 00:14:02,809
TAKE A PICTURE OF YOU.

362
00:14:02,809 --> 00:14:04,043
OKAY? TAKE A WALK.

363
00:14:05,378 --> 00:14:07,413
Mercedes: WALKING FOR CARMEN
WAS A BIG CHALLENGE,

364
00:14:07,413 --> 00:14:10,183
BECAUSE HE WANTED ELEGANCE,
HE WANTED DOMINANCE

365
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:11,517
AT THE SAME TIME.

366
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,286
HE WANTED IT TO BE VERY SMOOTH.

367
00:14:13,286 --> 00:14:15,355
Carmen: YOU DON'T HAVE
ENOUGH STRIDE.

368
00:14:15,355 --> 00:14:16,756
CAREFUL OF YOUR RIGHT ARM.

369
00:14:16,756 --> 00:14:18,558
IT'S LIKE A DEAD ARM.

370
00:14:18,558 --> 00:14:19,692
Shandi: SINCE I'VE NEVER
DONE THIS BEFORE,

371
00:14:19,692 --> 00:14:21,728
I'M REALLY UNSURE OF MYSELF,
AND I JUST NEED

372
00:14:21,728 --> 00:14:23,363
TO GET OVER THAT.

373
00:14:23,363 --> 00:14:25,264
Carmen: SHANDI--
SHE'S NOT COMFORTABLE

374
00:14:25,264 --> 00:14:26,666
IN HER OWN SHOES.

375
00:14:26,666 --> 00:14:28,501
SHE'S STILL VERY TIMID,
AND HER BODY LANGUAGE

376
00:14:28,501 --> 00:14:32,205
IS VERY, VERY INTROVERTED,
AND SHE NEEDS TO OVERCOME THAT.

377
00:14:32,205 --> 00:14:35,708
I THINK CAMILLE HAS
A PRETTY POWERFUL PRESENCE.

378
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:38,211
THAT'S ACTUALLY VERY GOOD.

379
00:14:38,211 --> 00:14:40,513
JENASCIA, NOT SO HEAVY
ON THE FEET.

380
00:14:40,513 --> 00:14:42,782
JUST GLIDE MORE.

381
00:14:42,782 --> 00:14:44,984
YOUR TURN--YOU LOOK LIKE
YOU WERE DOING A DOUBLE AXEL

382
00:14:44,984 --> 00:14:46,719
ON ICE SKATES OR SOMETHING.

383
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:47,520
DON'T BE AFRAID.

384
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,955
SEE, IT'S MOVING, ISN'T IT?

385
00:14:48,955 --> 00:14:51,357
YOANNA, IN MY OPINION,
HAS TO BUILD UP

386
00:14:51,357 --> 00:14:53,993
HER OWN SELF-CONFIDENCE
AND LEARN TO STAND

387
00:14:53,993 --> 00:14:55,161
A LITTLE BIT STRAIGHTER.

388
00:14:55,161 --> 00:14:59,198
♪♪♪

389
00:14:59,198 --> 00:15:00,166
Carmen: VERY GOOD.

390
00:15:00,166 --> 00:15:01,200
YOUR WALK WAS NICE.

391
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,402
YOUR ARMS WERE GOOD, TOO.

392
00:15:02,402 --> 00:15:04,604
WALK IT SLOWLY. VERY GOOD.

393
00:15:04,604 --> 00:15:06,873
COME BACK.

394
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:08,074
OKAY, BOTH SIDES.

395
00:15:08,074 --> 00:15:11,144
(trilling)
LIKE A TWIRLING DERVISH.

396
00:15:11,144 --> 00:15:12,412
Bethany: THE DRESS--
IT WAS SERIOUSLY

397
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:14,347
2 FEET TOO LONG.

398
00:15:14,347 --> 00:15:16,416
EVERYBODY ELSE HAD
THESE DRESSES THAT FIT.

399
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:18,751
Carmen: JUST PRETEND IT'S
THE WAY IT'S SUPPOSED TO BE.

400
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:19,719
Bethany: OKAY.

401
00:15:20,887 --> 00:15:22,555
Carmen: BETHANY LOOKED
REALLY GOOD.

402
00:15:22,555 --> 00:15:23,856
SHE LOOKED BEAUTIFUL
IN THE GOWN.

403
00:15:23,856 --> 00:15:25,925
SHE ACTUALLY CARRIED IT
WITH A LOT OF GRACE.

404
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:28,728
VERY, VERY GOOD. GREAT.

405
00:15:28,728 --> 00:15:30,096
Bethany: I HOPE THAT PEOPLE
WOULD STOP LOOKING AT MY TITS

406
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:32,165
AND START LOOKING
AT SOME TALENT HERE.

407
00:15:32,165 --> 00:15:35,067
Carmen: OKAY, LADIES, CAN I HAVE
YOUR ATTENTION, PLEASE?

408
00:15:35,067 --> 00:15:37,270
SHANDI, YOU WERE REALLY,
VERY, VERY STIFF.

409
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:38,971
YOU KNOW, YOU WERE LIKE
THE SHRINKING VIOLET,

410
00:15:38,971 --> 00:15:40,840
SO YOU NEED TO WORK ON THAT
A LITTLE BIT.

411
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:41,641
CATIE, RIGHT?

412
00:15:41,641 --> 00:15:43,242
Catie: YEAH.

413
00:15:43,242 --> 00:15:44,944
Carmen: VERY GRACEFUL.
Catie: THANK YOU.

414
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:46,746
Carmen: VERY NICE COMPOSURE
ON THE RUNWAY.

415
00:15:46,746 --> 00:15:48,381
I MEAN, YOU CAME OUT,
AND I WENT... (gasps)

416
00:15:48,381 --> 00:15:49,782
VERY, VERY NICE.
Catie: THANK YOU.

417
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:52,585
Carmen: YOANNA,
YOU'RE SO CONSCIOUS

418
00:15:52,585 --> 00:15:54,754
OF WHAT YOUR BODY'S DOING.

419
00:15:54,754 --> 00:15:57,723
IT'S LIKE YOU'RE NOT HAVING FUN
ON THE RUNWAY.

420
00:15:57,723 --> 00:15:59,358
IT ALL HAS TO DO
WITH CONFIDENCE,

421
00:15:59,358 --> 00:16:02,395
HOW YOU FEEL ABOUT YOURSELF,
AND PROJECTING THAT

422
00:16:02,395 --> 00:16:04,797
EITHER IN FRONT OF THE CAMERA
OR ON THE RUNWAY.

423
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:07,834
CAMILLE, WHEN YOU WERE DOWN
DOING YOUR PHOTO OP,

424
00:16:07,834 --> 00:16:12,004
YOU JUST MILKED THAT CAMERA
OVER AND OVER AGAIN

425
00:16:12,004 --> 00:16:13,639
AND DID NOT WANT TO LEAVE.

426
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:15,575
Camille: BECAUSE
THE LAST RUNWAY SHOW THAT I DID,

427
00:16:15,575 --> 00:16:17,009
THEY TOLD ME I DIDN'T SPEND
ENOUGH TIME AT THE END

428
00:16:17,009 --> 00:16:17,944
OF THE RUNWAY.

429
00:16:17,944 --> 00:16:19,278
Carmen: OHH.

430
00:16:19,278 --> 00:16:22,448
YOUR WALK IS A LITTLE--
IT'S A LITTLE SPORTSWEAR.

431
00:16:22,448 --> 00:16:24,116
SO YOU HAVE TO KEEP
YOUR COMPOSURE DOWN.

432
00:16:24,116 --> 00:16:26,419
Camille: SOMEONE THAT
TRAINED US HOW TO WALK--

433
00:16:26,419 --> 00:16:27,720
HE SAID WALK FAST.

434
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:29,755
Carmen: LISTEN TO WHAT
EVERYONE IS TELLING YOU...

435
00:16:29,755 --> 00:16:31,324
Camille: AND FIND
YOUR OWN MEDIUM.

436
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:32,391
Carmen: OR TEACHES YOU,
AND YOU HAVE TO FIND

437
00:16:32,391 --> 00:16:33,025
WHAT YOU'RE COMFORTABLE WITH.

438
00:16:33,025 --> 00:16:35,595
CAMILLE WAS A LITTLE AGGRESSIVE
IN THE SHOWROOM.

439
00:16:35,595 --> 00:16:37,263
SO I WAS LITTLE BIT...
(grunts)

440
00:16:37,263 --> 00:16:39,499
Mercedes: CAMILLE WASN'T
ACCEPTING HER RESPONSIBILITIES

441
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:41,834
OF MESSING UP, YOU KNOW?

442
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:43,369
JUST SAY, "OKAY. THANK YOU."

443
00:16:43,369 --> 00:16:45,137
Yoanna: I WAS JUST KIND OF
EMBARRASSED, BECAUSE WE WERE

444
00:16:45,137 --> 00:16:47,840
GUESTS IN HIS SHOWROOM,
AND I THOUGHT IT WAS TACKY.

445
00:16:51,210 --> 00:16:54,247
Carmen: IT WAS NOT, UM,
AN EASY DECISION FOR ME TO MAKE.

446
00:16:54,247 --> 00:16:55,548
YOU DID A GREAT JOB.

447
00:16:55,548 --> 00:16:58,684
SO I'M GOING TO PICK
WHOM I THINK DID THE BEST JOB,

